From 0c8e70fc45607e1ac9cb0b2e2daa6c2659b84fce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:02:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/28] WIP norm: port the narrow-row RMS norm fusion

Ports the other solution's norm-gated.cu: a wave-per-row RMS norm for narrow
rows (ncols <= 256, >= 4096 rows) that processes 8 rows per 256-thread block
instead of the one-block-per-row rms_norm_f32<256>, which is block-scheduling
bound for the model's per-head norms.  Two matchers, wired in ggml_cuda_try_fuse
before the generic RMS_NORM+MUL fusion, plus the gated-variant alloc deps:
  * norm_gated: RMS_NORM -> MUL(w) -> [view*|MUL_MAT] -> SIGMOID -> MUL, one
    kernel (also fuses the gate arithmetic the separate sigmoid+mul did);
  * norm_rows:  plain RMS_NORM -> MUL(w).

The reduction order is identical to rms_norm_f32<256,...> + block_reduce (per-warp
xor trees over 32 consecutive columns, then a xor tree over the 8 partials padded
with zeros) and the gate is the same 1/(1+expf(-z)), so the result is bit-identical.

Default ON (per the default-on policy); GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_NORM_ROWS=1 is the A/B
kill switch.

gfx1151, qwen4exp IQ4_NL:
  * width probe PASS (worst maxdiff 0); row0 logits hash identical on/off;
    same-seed greedy text identical (765 chars sha=f61199ba5644) on/off.
  * kernel profile (pp8192, ub8192): rms_norm_f32<256,true> 282.8 + the gated
    sigmoid/mul -> rms_rows_f32<true> 210.5 + rms_rows_f32<false> 77.4 ms.
  * A/B at -b/-ub 4096 (the memory-safe protocol; see the ubatch note in
    wip/closing-the-gap): pp8192 1222.74 -> 1226.09, pp32768 1166.13 -> 1169.37
    (+~0.3 %, consistent sign).

Exported to wip/closing-the-gap/patches/0006.
